    "text": "Step 2: Evaluate \\( f(\\sqrt{45}) \\).\n\nFirst, calculate \\(\\sqrt{45}\\). Since \\(45 = 9 \\times 5\\) and \\(\\sqrt{9} = 3\\), we have:\n\\[ \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\times 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}. \\]\nApproximating \\(\\sqrt{5} \\approx 2.236\\), we get:\n\\[ \\sqrt{45} \\approx 3 \\times 2.236 = 6.708. \\]\nSince \\(6.708 \\geq 4\\), we use the first part of the piecewise function:\n\\[ f(\\sqrt{45}) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{45} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 6.708 \\rfloor = 6. \\]"
